			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Add lint allowances to build script for generated bindings\n\nPreserve build stability by re-allowing standard naming and usage lints (`non_snake_case`, `dead_code`, etc.) within `build.rs`. This compensates for the recent global removal of `#![allow(non_snake_case)]` across the source tree, which inadvertently flagged warnings in build scripts consuming auto-generated protocol bindings or external definitions.\n\nThe change ensures the build process remains clean while the main application source maintains strict PascalCase compliance and active linting. This aligns with the pattern in `Source/Vine/Generated/mod.rs` where specific allowances are retained for non-manual code.",
			"SHA": "f520c6044f6940106f177b01327ed613e11f7846"
		},
