			],
			"Message": "style(Mountain): Remove pervasive leading empty lines after module doc comments\n\nStrip the redundant single empty line immediately following `//! ...` module doc comments across over 400 files in the Mountain backend. This affects Air integration, Binary entry points, Command handlers, Environment providers, ExtensionManagement, and the full IPC layer (WindServiceHandlers, RPC/CocoonService, Track, Vine).\n\nThe change enforces a tighter file header style where documentation blocks are directly followed by the first code declaration or `use` statement, eliminating stylistic noise while preserving all logic and API contracts. `Source/Library.rs` retain necessary global allowances for generated code, while the rest of the source tree now adheres to a uniform header structure.\n\nRefs #CLAUDE.md",
			"SHA": "2a4878c8f2eebf57350b1ee6725633c2d3199a53"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
