			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove pervasive dead_code and unused_imports allowances\n\nStrip `#![allow(dead_code, unused_imports, unused_variables)]` and related lint suppressions from over 200 files across the Mountain backend. This cleanup spans the Air integration, ApplicationState, Binary entry points, ExtensionManagement, IPC layers (WindServiceHandlers, Vine, TauriIPC, SecureChannel), RPC services (Cocoon, Echo, Workspace), Telemetry, Track, and Update modules.\n\nRemove redundant `#[allow(dead_code)]` and `#[allow(unused_imports)]` attributes from structs, constants, traits, functions, and module-level declarations. Also normalize file headers by removing leading empty lines and unused import groups to align with the project-wide PascalCase and strict linting standards.\n\nEnsure `Source/Library.rs` retains only necessary global allowances for generated code and external bindings, while `Source/Binary/Main/Entry.rs` and build scripts are updated to reflect the new strict lint policy. This change eliminates style noise from reviews and ensures future code additions adhere to the required naming and usage conventions.\n\nRefs #CLAUDE.md",
			"SHA": "350d161450f66626001a72885bfde33237ae9dfd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T03:05:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove Vine generated allow attributes for naming lints\n\nStrip `non_snake_case` and `non_camel_case_types` allowances from `Source/Vine/Generated/mod.rs`. This aligns the auto-generated gRPC protocol bindings with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention enforced across the codebase, removing the previous suppression of warnings for protocol-specific identifiers.\n\nThe `clippy::all`, `unused_imports`, and `unused_qualifications` allowances are retained as they remain necessary for generated code where manual optimization is not feasible. This change ensures that only relevant lints are suppressed, improving code quality checks for the generated IPC layer.",
			"SHA": "b6c715ff7d8ce7db7909dc65ca482856a2bdd5b3"
		},
