				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove pervasive leading empty lines across Source\n\nStrip the redundant single empty line immediately following the module doc comment in over 400 Rust source files. This includes the Air integration client, ApplicationState persistence and recovery layers, Binary entry points (DNS, TLS, PostHog), Cache subsystems, Command handlers, IPC bridges (Vine, WindServiceAdapters, StatusReporter), RPC services (Cocoon, Echo, Workspace), and Runtime shutdown logic.\n\nThe change consolidates the pattern where `//! ...` comments are followed by a blank line before the first `use` or `struct` declaration, enforcing a tighter, more consistent file header style. No logic, types, or public APIs are modified; the diff is purely cosmetic whitespace normalization.\n\nThis unifies the formatting style across the Mountain codebase, removing stylistic noise from reviews and ensuring the file structure remains uniform regardless of the specific module or feature.\n\nRefs #CLAUDE.md",
			"SHA": "58c1911fec75324953e6b953ff369ea99ef4bcf4"
		}
